e-iT® DEAD Green™ viability stain cannot occur in live cells due to the impermeability of the plasma membrane to the stain. Drugs and test compounds that lead to serious cell injuries, including plasma membrane permeability, allow entry of the Image-iT® DEAD Green™ viability stain, enabling discrimination of dead cells. Hoechst 33342, which stains nuclear DNA in live and dead cells, is included in the kit as a segmentation tool for automated image analysis.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":600.6908559150656,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":36.3056,"r":290.2911999999999,"t":710.2416999999999},"charspan":[0,648],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"a cell-impermeant, nonfluorescent, high-affinity DNA stain that forms highly fluorescent and stable dye-nucleic acid complexes when bound to DNA. Thus, staining of nuclear DNA by the Image-iT® DEAD Green™ viability stain cannot occur in live cells due to the impermeability of the plasma membrane to the stain. Drugs and test compounds that lead to serious cell injuries, including plasma membrane permeability, allow entry of the Image-iT® DEAD Green™ viability stain, enabling discrimination of dead cells. Hoechst 33342, which stains nuclear DNA in live and dead cells, is included in the kit as a segmentation tool for automated image analysis."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The HCS DNA Damage Kit contains sufficient material to perform the DNA damage assay on two 96-well plates when used as described in the protocol provided:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":567.6908559150656,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":36.3056,"r":290.2648,"t":600.2416999999999},"charspan":[0,154],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The HCS DNA Damage Kit contains sufficient material to perform the DNA damage assay on two 96-well plates when used as described in the protocol provided:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":false,"label":"list_item","marker":"·","