use multiple approaches to study cytotoxicity.    In  addition  to  the  HCS  DNA  Damage  Kit,  we  offer  the  HCS LIVE/DEAD® Green Kit (H10290) and the HCS Mitochondrial Health Kit (H10295), both of which employ the Image-iT® DEAD™ Green viability stain.  Additionally, the HCS LIVE/DEAD® Kit provides a choice of two nucleic acid stains-the far-red-fluorescent HCS NuclearMask™ Deep Red stain (H10294, Section 12.5) and the blue-fluorescent Hoechst 33342 (H1399, H3570, H21492; Section 12.5)-for use as cell-permeant nuclear segmentation tools. The HCS Mitochondrial Health Kit provides Image-iT® DEAD Green viability stain and Hoechst 33342 stain, as well as the MitoHealth stain, which accumulates in the mitochondria of live cells in proportion to the mitochondrial membrane potential. Both of these kits provide sufficient reagents to perform the assays on two 96-well plates, using the protocol provided.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":369.69085591506575,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":36.3056,"r":290.333528,"t":490.2417},"charspan":[0,747],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":666.6908559150656,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":303.30559999999997,"r":557.3,"t":710.2416999999999},"charspan":[748,1008],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"Because no single parameter fully defines cell viability in all systems, it is often useful to use multiple approaches to study cytotoxicity.    In  addition  to  the  HCS  DNA  Damage  Kit,  we  offer  the  HCS LIVE/DEAD® Green Kit (H10290) and the HCS Mitochondrial Health Kit (H10295), both of which employ the Image-iT® DEAD™ Green viability stain.  Additionally, the HCS LIVE/DEAD® Kit provides a choice of two nucleic acid stains-the far-red-fluorescent HCS NuclearMask™ Deep Red stain (H10294, Section 12.5) and the blue-fluorescent Hoechst 33342 (H1399, H3570, H21492; Section 12.5)-for use as cell-permeant nuclear segmentation tools. The HCS Mitochondrial Health Kit provides Image-iT® DEAD Green viability stain and Hoechst 33342 stain, as well as the MitoHealth stain, which accumulates in the mitochondria of live cells in proportion to the mitochondrial membrane potential. Both of these kits provide sufficient reagents to perform the assays on two 96-well plates, using the protocol provided."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"O","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":305.0356241069519,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":154.8151,"r":159.862764,"t":311.375892},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"O"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"O","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":336.59962410695186,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":154.8151,"r":159.862764,"t":342.939892},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/11","text":"O"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"HO","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":326.07472410695186,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":131.9441,"r":141.6761,"t":332.414992},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/12","text":"HO"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"(CH3CH2)2N","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":288.7250241069519,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":78.3056,"r":114.16653600000001,"t":295.065292},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/13","text":"(CH3CH2)2N"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"CH2","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":325.3374430802139,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":191.4732,"r":203.545096,"t":332.414992},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/14","text":"CH2"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"(CH2)3�O3","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":335.8551430802139,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":205.5607,"r":236.741896,"t":342.939892},"charspan":[0,9],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/15","text":"(CH2)3�O3"},{"children":[],"content_la